085,\"color\":\"#ffcf9e\",\"strength\":30,\"point_lights\":1,\"light_w\":12}},{\"type\":\"table_cluster\",\"name\":\"Table_12\",\"rect\":[-2.05,7.93,-2.03,7.95],\"z\":1.8,\"rows\":1,\"cols\":1,\"jitter\":0.0,\"seed\":12,\"table_radius\":0.3,\"table_height\":0.9,\"table_material\":\"table\",\"lamp\":{\"height\":0.22,\"radius\":0.085,\"color\":\"#ffcf9e\",\"strength\":30,\"point_lights\":1,\"light_w\":12}},{\"type\":\"table_cluster\",\"name\":\"Table_13\",\"rect\":[-2.63,9.15,-2.61,9.17],\"z\":2.4,\"rows\":1,\"cols\":1,\"jitter\":0.0,\"seed\":13,\"table_radius\":0.35,\"table_height\":0.7,\"table_material\":\"table\",\"lamp\":{\"height\":0.22,\"radius\":0.085,\"color\":\"#ffcf9e\",\"strength\":30,\"point_lights\":1,\"light_w\":12}},{\"type\":\"table_cluster\",\"name\":\"Table_14\",\"rect\":[-0.23,9.25,-0.21,9.27],\"z\":2.4,\"rows\":1,\"cols\":1,\"jitter\":0.0,\"seed\":14,\"table_radius\":0.35,\"table_height\":0.9,\"table_material\":\"table\",\"lamp\":{\"height\":0.22,\"radius\":0.085,\"color\":\"#ffcf9e\",\"strength\":30,\"point_lights\":1,\"light_w\":12}},{\"type\":\"table_cluster\",\"name\":\"Table_15\",\"rect\":[-2.96,10.13,-2.94,10.15],\"z\":2.4,\"rows\":1,\"cols\":1,\"jitter\":0.0,\"seed\":15,\"table_radius\":0.35,\"table_height\":1.06,\"table_material\":\"table\",\"lamp\":{\"height\":0.22,\"radius\":0.085,\"color\":\"#ffcf9e\",\"strength\":30,\"point_lights\":1,\"light_w\":12}},{\"type\":\"table_cluster\",\"name\":\"Table_16\",\"rect\":[6.05,12.76,6.07,12.78],\"z\":1.2,\"rows\":1,\"cols\":1,\"jitter\":0.0,\"seed\":16,\"table_radius\":0.35,\"table_height\":0.9,\"table_material\":\"table\",\"lamp\":{\"height\":0.22,\"radius\":0.085,\"color\":\"#ffcf9e\",\"strength\":30,\"point_lights\":1,\"light_w\":12}}],\"characters\":{\"DS\":{\"location\":[-0.46,-7.285,4.05],\"facing_target\":[-0.46,0.0,5.5],\"height_m\":1.58,\"lean_note\":\"VIP balcony prow (floor z 4.05), 0.14 m to the -X side of the prow's right corner post at (-0.32,-7.105). SHOT 1: face-box centre F = (-0.46,-7.185,5.50) = feet + (0,+0.10,+1.45); the chrome handrail (top z 5.115, axis y -7.105) is 0.08 m in front of F and 0.385 m below it; forearms crossed on it, torso tipped 5-10 deg forward. SHOT 2: same feet, but she leans over the rail to watch the stage: head ~0.4 m further toward the pit (head centre near (-0.5,-6.8,5.35); this is where the shot-2 solve puts her hair bow, and it puts her hair at the left frame edge at rows 200-1000 in f303), right forearm on the rail with the wrist at its visible left end (about (-0.33,-7.10,5.12)). An upright stand-in at the root blocks CAM_Shot2 for f149-f260; hide it for shot 2.\"},\"CL\":{\"location\":[0.12,0.42,0.15],\"facing_target\":[-0.46,-7.185,5.5],\"height_m\":1.6,\"lean_note\":\"On the stage disc (r 0.85, top z 0.15), 0.44 m behind its centre toward +Y, facing DS's balcony. Position from the shot-2 head-blob anchors (blob = point 1.40 m above the feet; rms 11 px over f199-f300) and the skirt hem on the lit disc in f250-f303. Same spot in shot 3.\"}},\"notes\":[\"VENUE (one coherent model, metres, origin = stage-disc centre on the pit floor): hall x -8.2..+8.2, y -12.0..+14.0, flat ceiling z 9.5. Sunken dance pit z 0 for |x|<=3.2, y -8.15..+4.4 with the stage disc r 0.85 / top 0.15 at the origin. Behind the pit (+Y) a 4-tier lounge bank: treads 1.5 m deep, rise 0.6 m (tier tops 0.6/1.2/1.8/2.4 at y 4.4-5.9/5.9-7.4/7.4-8.9/8.9-10.4, |x|<=4.7). Side terraces: z 0.6 for 3.2<|x|<=4.4 and z 1.2 for |x|>4.4 (y -8.15..4.4), corner lounges z 1.2 for |x|>4.7, y>4.4. U-shaped mezzanine gallery on back and both sides: floor 4.48, fascia band 3.80-4.48, 1.05 m glass balustrade with chrome top rail (z 5.55, posts 1.6 m), soffit downlights every 0.8 m, wall sconces at z 5.92 on the back wall (y 14). At the rear the gallery front (y 10.3) is set back behind the top tier: a 1.4 m riser wall with vertical mirror slats (z 2.45-3.75, every 0.4 m) is what shows under the fascia at f303 upper right. The side galleries overhang the side terraces; their front runs from the back corner (+-4.7,10.3) inward 6.7 deg to (+-4.0,4.3), then straight along y to the balcony end.\",\"DS's VIP BALCONY (-Y end): floor z 4.05 (0.43 m below the gallery ring - a sunken VIP box), slab 0.3 m, spanning the hall width for y<-8.15 plus a trapezoidal prow: front segment along X at y -7.105 from x -2.32 to -0.32, wings at +-26.4 deg back to y -8.15 / x -4.0. Chrome tube handrail dia 0.032 m, top z 5.115 (1.065 m above the floor), bottle-shaped clamp posts at <=1.0 m (one exactly at the right prow corner), frameless glass panels 0.965 m tall under it (top edge 0.04 m below the tube top). The pit front wall under the balcony is at y -8.15..-8.45. Behind DS: VIP lounge 4.8 m deep - two low sofas (y -10.5..-9.85), three low lounge tables with small warm lamps (y ~-9.35), a banquette along the window, a full-height window wall at y -12.0 with mullions every 2.4 m (one at x -1.66) and a transom at 7.6, and a 190x85 m emissive city-skyline plane 150 m out (y -150) so its image scale changes <0.5% during the shot-1 dolly.\",\"SCALE CHAIN: all metric positions are in CAM_Shot2's frame (s2cam/shot2_path.json, stage at origin, CL 1.60 m, crowd 1.6-1.65 m). Far architecture was placed on the rays of measured image features; its depth comes from size cues (table-lamp shade dia ~0.17 m = seated-head width, table tops ~0.7-0.8 m) plus a buildable tier section. If CAM_Shot2 is re-solved with a different scale or path, re-run the placement (scratchpad/arch/tables4.py, geometry.py) rather than editing numbers by hand.\",\"SHOT-1 RIG: CAM_Shot1 was solved with an assumed face point F_old (0,-8.0,4.95). In this venue DS's face point is F = (-0.46,-7.185,5.50), so translate every CAM_Shot1 location, target and DOF focus by (-0.46,+0.815,+0.55). No rotation is needed: DS's rail segment runs along X, perpendicular to the dolly. Checked: rail top within 7 px at f1, the shot-1 clamp post lands on the prow corner post (1 px), the dark mullion within 8 px, DS face point within 3-9 px of the face-box centres.\",\"TABLES: 17 cocktail/lounge tables (Table_00..16, sorted by y) were placed one per measured lamp by intersecting the lamp ray (f303, f280, f250, f230, f210, f200, f185, f170, f160) with the tier surface and solving the table height (0.4-1.2 m) so the lamp lands exactly on its ray; lamps seen in several frames were merged. Reprojection over 90 lamp observations in 11 shot-2 frames: median 3.1 px, p90 6.7 px. Pit-level tables at (2.57,4.01) and (2.90,0.82) are tall standing tables at the right edge of the dance floor - keep the crowd 0.5 m away from them.\",\"CROWD FLOOR LEVELS (for the crowd owner): pit z 0 rect [-3.0,-6.8,3.0,4.2] minus the stage circle [0,0,1.15] and the two pit tables; back tiers z 0.6/1.2/1.8/2.4 in y bands 4.4-5.9/5.9-7.4/7.4-8.9/8.9-10.4 (|x|<4.5, keep 0.45 m off table centres; mostly seated on tiers 2-4); right/left terrace z 0.6 (3.3<|x|<4.3) and z 1.2 (|x| 4.5-8.0); galleries z 4.48 (people visible behind the glass in f185-f230: rect [-4.5,10.6,4.5,13.6] and side strips 4.2<|x|<8.0); VIP lounge z 4.05 rect [-3.4,-11.2,2.4,-8.4] (shot-1 guests, mostly seated, face heights 1.15-1.30 m).\",\"SPOTLIGHT RIG: lighting truss across the ceiling at y 2.63, z 9.1 with five fixtures. The single white beam seen from f170 to f303 fits a straight line through the stage-disc centre with direction (0.039,0.30,1): the source is up and 2.6 m behind the stage (+Y side) and the beam tilts 17 deg from vertical toward the balcony (11 px rms over 7 frames); the main fixture 'SpotFixture' sits on that line at (0.34,2.63,8.8). A SPOT at (0.34,2.63,8.6) aimed at (0,0,0.15) with a ~12 deg cone reproduces the r~0.8 m lit pool (measured r 0.78 at z 0.15 in f250/f260/f280). The source height is not observable; any point on that line works.\",\"SHOT-3 RE-AIM: the shot-3 fragment assumed CL at (0,0) on a 0.3 m stage. With CL feet at (0.12,0.42,0.15), keep CAM_Shot3 at (-0.3,-7.6,5.55), aim it so the point 1.45 m above her feet, (0.12,0.42,1.60), lands at (566,491), and use lens ~247 mm (8.95 m to that point). Behind her knees the camera then sees the pit floor 0.9-1.4 m behind her (beyond the r 0.85 disc), i.e. dark glossy blue floor, as in the source.\",\"LAMP-SIZE CHEAT: the AI image stacks the left table rows more steeply than any buildable bank, so in the rebuilt set the upper-row lamps (tiers 3-4) are 15-25% smaller on screen than in the source. If that matters, raise lamp.radius and lamp.height of Table_10..Table_15 (tiers 3-4) by ~1.2x; positions already match.\"]}", "measurements": [{"name": "stage disc centre", "value": "(0.02, 0.03) at z 0.15 (taken as origin)", "unit": "m", "method": "lit-pool mask (V>150, S<110, CL masked) in f250/f260/f280, convex hull back-projected through CAM_Shot2 to z 0.15, robust circle fit; three frames agree within 0.06 m", "confidence": 0.7}, {"name": "stage disc radius", "value": "0.85 (lit pool fit 0.78)", "unit": "m", "method": "same hull circle fit gives r 0.78 in all three frames; widened to 0.85 so CL (0.44 m behind centre, skirt ~0.3 m) stays on it; model ellipse in f260 spans x 415-776 / y 1179-1393 vs pool 427-761 / 1200-1389", "confidence": 0.6}, {"name": "stage height", "value": "0.15", "unit": "m", "method": "no riser edge visible; crowd stands flush at the pool edge; CL image height 283 px in f303 fits 0-0.3 m equally (280-297 px), so a low platform is assumed", "confidence": 0.3}, {"name": "CL root", "value": "(0.12, 0.42, 0.15)", "unit": "m", "method": "skirt hem at (640,1172) in f303 back-projected to the disc top plus skirt offset; shot-2 head-blob anchors fit with a point 1.40 m above the feet (rms 11.6 px over 21 frames)", "confidence": 0.6}, {"name": "pit extent", "value": "|x|<=3.2, y -8.15..+4.4, z 0", "unit": "m", "method": "standing heads (z 1.6) at rows 565-640 in f303 back-project to y 3.3-4.8; f303 frame edges at y~0 reach x -2.9..+1.8; pit front wall under the balcony prow", "confidence": 0.5}, {"name": "b